meta {
  name: Update User Branch Permissions
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users/manage/{{manageUserId}}/branch-permissions
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "branchId": "{{branchId}}",
    "items": [
      {
        "moduleKey": "lab_operations",
        "permissionKey": "lab_operations:view",
        "allowed": true
      },
      {
        "moduleKey": "lab_operations",
        "permissionKey": "lab_operations:enter_results",
        "allowed": true
      },
      {
        "moduleKey": "lab_operations",
        "permissionKey": "lab_operations:verify",
        "allowed": false
      },
      {
        "permissionKey": "sales:edit",
        "moduleKey": "sales",
        "allowed": false
      },
      {
        "moduleKey": "pharmacy",
        "permissionKey": "pharmacy:view",
        "allowed": false
      }
    ]
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  manageUserId: ac2f40e0-4420-4b12-a866-1fe773f58aeb
  branchId: d3b91f75-b897-4c81-b216-48bde7d2aad1
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires ANY of `business_admin:user_management__update_the_user_permissions`, `branch_admin:user_management__update_the_user_permissions_for_assigned_branch` — enforced by `PermissionGuard` (`@RequirePermission` / `@RequireAnyPermission`). A caller whose effective permissions (user override ?? branch-role override ?? role baseline) lack this get **403 `PERMISSION_DENIED`**; the `business_admin` / `administrator` roles bypass all checks, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` (an admin) still succeeds here.
  
  Replace the (user + branch) permission grants. The client sends the full set
  for the branch (supports Select-All / Deselect-All per module). Only modules
  **enabled for the branch** are accepted, and each `permissionKey` must belong
  to its `moduleKey` (else 422 INVALID_MODULE_KEY / MODULE_NOT_ENABLED_FOR_BRANCH).
  Absent permissions fall back to the role baseline.
}
